I don't think this is interesting for Gehennom (that you presumed above).
On no-teleport levels you can always zap away the offender, or, if you are
surrounded, break a wand of teleportation (preferable a single charged
wand). Taking a scroll of levelport out of your bag is just one additional
step if you really want to leave. And you should always remember that some
monsters follow you if you leave the level by level teleport, thus it's
not always an emergency escape as you'd expect. Another option for Gehennom
is just digging down (which is almost everywhere possible there, but with
the same caveat of accompanying offenders as with level-teleportation).

